{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792280000000-review-6b-task-transport.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-12 23:45 +07\n# Review (mutation method): slice 6b, lift-task / lower-task and the safepoint harness\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b`, branch `srvm-phase6b`, commit c3d37586 (`git diff master...HEAD`). Spec: `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` sections 3-8 (5.2 row table, 6.3, 7, 7.1, 8.2 acceptance 1-9). Engineer report (opus, so you are the non-author reviewer): `collab/1792270000000-engineer-6b-task-transport.report.md`. Check: (1) does `lift-task`/`lower-task` in `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` implement section 7 (lift: safepoint refusals, pending rows, free-env default from the retained field with explicit override, source-index tree association, dependency closure; lower: decode order, ALL refusals before ANY attach, attach once per stream identity, code by address A only, values re-sealed, nothing runs, install children, free env as :env and :free-env); (2) the engineer's deviations 1-10 and design bugs B1-B4: accept or object each, and say which design text must change (the Architect will amend the design; give exact section and wording hints); (3) the harness: 89 runs really are distinct (22 wrapped rows x 4 segments + 1), laws 1-3 and 6 actually asserted, the stream correspondence fixture cannot make law 2 vacuous; (4) portability read for Node and Dart (no `for` over long seqs, no private var access, multi-key assoc on nil, unary minus, catches, `fn?`/`cbor/numeric?` on Dart) and the `handoff.cljc` `(symbol (str m \"/\" x))` latent bug the engineer flagged (verify; do not edit); (5) the `store-write-audit` allowlist additions: justified? (6) your own mutants (back up with cp, verify restore by diff and git diff --quiet): lower attaches before the last refusal; lift serves before the safepoint refusal; free-env override ignored; tail state keeps a window; pending ready-queue not required empty; duplicate attach for one stream identity; install child not restored; values not re-sealed; closure computed before the walk. Say which survive. Run `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` and `-i :slow` for the matrix, foreground only. Findings file `collab/1792280000000-review-6b-task-transport.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` ending VERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE or CHANGES_REQUESTED, findings table with severity and file:line. Edit nothing else.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
