{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '989,1040p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; sed -n '1095,1130p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '570,594p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; rg -n 'resolve-var|resolve-module|env-store-of' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc; sed -n '360,436p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc; sed -n '956,984p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"\n### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n\n**DECIDED** (ruling 4). No vector is projected to datoms; the direct\nload path is the only path (§10.4).\n\n### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\n\n**DECIDED** by the review's finding and §4.4. The task's initial free\nenvironment travels **once, explicitly**, as the root's `free-env`\nslot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\ncomplete map and is checked by rules X1 and E2. On lower, the\nsemantic-register kernel receives it as the machine's base `:env`\n(`create-vm`'s `:env` option, `semantic_register.cljc:261`); a de Bruijn\nkernel receives it as its `:free-env` (`stack.cljc:418`) and\nreconstructs positional frames from each `E` by the chain (§4.4).\n\n**Where the lift gets it (PROPOSED, the gap the review named).** It is\n**never recovered from a current `E`** (§4.4). Its source is, per\nkernel:\n\n- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n\nMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\nusually already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Lift and lower\n\n### 7.1 Lift\n  (let [slots (:slots task) code-map (nth slots 11)\n        free-env (decode-keyed (nth slots 5) decoded-value)\n        waits (nth slots 13)\n        ffi-ids (into #{} (keep (fn [w]\n                                  (let [[_ p] (:slots w) [reason & xs] (:slots p)]\n                                    (case reason :ffi (second xs) :ffi-request (first xs) nil)))) waits)\n        ctx {:free-env free-env :ffi-call-ids ffi-ids}]\n    (letfn [(judge\n              [n context context-map path]\n              (when-let [d (frame/defect (decode-frame n decoded-value) code-map context context-map)]\n                (-> d (assoc :yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable)\n                    (update :yin.k/path #(into path %)))))\n            (captures\n              [n path]\n              (if (= :reified (:kind n))\n                (or (judge (first (:slots n)) :captured ctx path)\n                    (captures (first (:slots n)) (conj path 0)))\n                (some (fn [[i d x]]\n                        (cond\n                          (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (validate-frames x)\n                          (ref? d) (captures x (conj path i))\n                          (refs? d) (some (fn [[j child]] (captures child (conj path i j))) (map-indexed vector x))\n                          (and (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d) (= :row (first x))) (captures (second x) (conj path i))\n                          :else nil))\n                      (map vector (range) (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n)))))]\n      (or\n        (when-let [d (frame/task-defect ctx)] (assoc d :yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable))\n        (some (fn [[i w]] (judge w :wait ctx [:frames i])) (map-indexed vector waits))\n        (some (fn [[p state]] (judge state :parked (assoc ctx :parked-key p) [:parked p]))\n              (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8))))\n        (captures task [])))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Task transport (continuation design §7): lift-task and lower-task\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest install-rows-carry-the-child\n  (doseq [[n phase] [[10 :parked] [11 :running] [12 :parked]]]\n    (testing (str \"row \" n)\n      (let [world (bare n)\n            {:keys [serve! toy]} (served #{:reader})\n            wire (rows/lift-task (:machine world) serve! (lift-opts))\n            [install] (slot (root-task wire) 12)\n            [mn carried-phase _ _ child] (:slots install)\n            recv (rows/lower-task (machine {:attach-stream (s/attacher toy)}) wire (s/attacher toy))\n            inst (get-in recv [:installs 'host.mod])\n            lowered (:vm inst)]\n        (is (= 'host.mod mn))\n        (is (= phase carried-phase) \"the child's phase as the source held it\")\n        (is (= :blocked (slot child 2)) \"the child's kind\")\n        (is (= :child (slot child 3)))\n        (is (= [:install 'host.mod] (:slots (first-pending (root-task wire)))))\n        (is (= phase (:phase inst)))\n        (is (nil? (:control lowered)) \"no initialization on lower: nothing runs\")\n        (is (= [:next] (mapv :reason (:wait-set lowered))) \"the child waits where it was lifted\")\n        (is (vm/blocked? lowered))\n        (is (= (count (slot child 11)) (count (:code-aliases lowered))) \"the child's code by A\")))))\n\n\n(deftest captures\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:24:     dispatch and `resolve-var` read a supplied registry rather than a global.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:115:(defn resolve-var\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:134:                            (module/resolve-module\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:183:(defn env-store-of\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:202:  (or (:store-of state) (env-store-of (:env state))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:291:;; and writes only that table; no store instruction and no `resolve-var`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1494:      (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:152:                                 (engine/resolve-var E\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:153:                                                     (engine/active-store machine (engine/env-store-of E))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:166:                                                          (engine/env-store-of E) (nth inst 2) value)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:171:                                (assoc W (nth inst 1) (get (engine/active-store machine (engine/env-store-of E)) (nth inst 2)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:174:                                                             (engine/env-store-of E) (nth inst 2) (nth inst 3))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc:438:          store-of (engine/env-store-of env)]\n     :call-in       explicit inbound request handle\n     :call-out      explicit outbound response handle\n     :call-out-cursor, :ffi-caller-id  `yin.vm/empty-state`'s\n     :call-capacity capacity for a constructed FFI pair\n     :bridge        host FFI handlers\n\n   As for the walker: there is no `:in-stream` (program observation belongs\n   to `dao.stream.observer`), and construction is all-or-nothing — the FFI\n   pair and its call-out cursor are stream operations whose failure fails\n   here.\"\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (when (contains? opts :in-stream)\n     (throw (ex-info\n              \"Program observation moved to dao.stream.observer: a VM no longer accepts :in-stream\"\n              {:in-stream (:in-stream opts)})))\n   (let [env (vm/check-bindings! :env (or (:env opts) {}))\n         base (vm/empty-state\n                (assoc (select-keys opts\n                                    [:primitives :primitive-profiles\n                                     :primitive-canonical-names :modules\n                                     :make-stream :call-in :call-out\n                                     :call-out-cursor :ffi-caller-id\n                                     :call-capacity :link-request\n                                     :link-response :origin :ancestry\n                                     :capability-secret :secret-source\n                                     :attach-stream :gc-threshold])\n                       :telemetry (:telemetry opts)\n                       :vm-model :semantic-register))]\n     (-> (map->RegisterVM (merge base\n                                 {:bridge nil,\n                                  :program nil,\n                                  :control nil,\n                                  :env env,\n                                  :free-env env,\n                                  :window {},\n                                  :k nil,\n                                  :value nil,\n                                  :code {},\n                                  :code-aliases {},\n                                  :halted? true,\n                                  :blocked? false}))\n         (telemetry/install :semantic-register)\n         (ffi/attach (:bridge opts))\n         (telemetry/emit-snapshot :init)))))\n\n\n(extend-type RegisterVM\n  module/IModuleKernel\n  (link-format [_]\n    {:format :yin.semantic-register/code, :contract code/contract})\n  (spawn-module\n    [vm image {:keys [modules origin ancestry capability-secret]}]\n    (load-vector (create-vm\n                   {:primitives (:primitives vm),\n                    :primitive-profiles (:primitive-profiles vm),\n                    :primitive-canonical-names (:primitive-canonical-names vm),\n                    :modules modules,\n                    :make-stream (:make-stream vm),\n                    :link-request (get (:resources vm)\n                                       module/link-request-resource),\n                    :link-response (get (:resources vm)\n                                        module/link-response-resource),\n                    :origin origin,\n                    :ancestry ancestry,\n                    :capability-secret capability-secret,\n                    :secret-source (:secret-source vm),\n                    :attach-stream (:attach-stream vm),\n                    :gc-threshold (:base (:gc vm))})\n                 image\n                 code/contract))\n  (image-identity [_ image] (jing/segment-key image))\n  (image-holds? [_ image segment] (jing/segment-matches? segment image))\n  (attach-module [vm image] (attach-image vm image code/contract))\n  (lift-closure [vm closure encode]\n    (let [local (:segment closure)\n          address (some (fn [[a l]] (when (= l local) a)) (:code-aliases vm))\n(defn canonical-under\n  \"Test-only §5.5 re-emission under an explicit stream correspondence.\n   Missing marker coverage fails; neither traversal order nor original\n   cursor-cell numbering chooses a logical identity. Accepts a carrier.\"\n  [wire correspondence]\n  (let [task (decode* wire (assoc default-budget :check-numbering false))]\n    (letfn [(rewrite-slot\n              [d x]\n              (cond (ref? d) (rewrite x) (refs? d) (mapv rewrite x)\n                    (and (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d) (= :row (first x))) [:row (rewrite (second x))]\n                    :else x))\n            (rewrite\n              [n]\n              (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n                (if (= :stream kind)\n                  (let [id (first slots)]\n                    (when-not (contains? correspondence id) (bad! :missing-stream-correspondence [id]))\n                    (node :stream [(get correspondence id) (get correspondence id)]))\n                  (node kind (mapv rewrite-slot (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n      (emit (rewrite task)))))\n\n\n(defn- value-node\n  [x]\n  (check-literal-markers! x)\n  [:lit x])\n\n\n(defn- decoded-value\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
